/*  EXPECTED: REJECTED at type-check, identically by both backends.
    A function stores what it is given into a `permanently` series, and is cast in a rabbit on one of
    the rabbit's series.

    A constant lives as long as the program, so a store into one is judged wherever the function
    is cast (docs/SOUNDNESS.md, *Open*, closed 2026-11-25). */

Define table as a series of series of number permanently.
Bind void to add-row, given (the series of number r):
    Insert r into table.
Done.
Pull a rabbit.
    Define xs as a series of number with (3, 2).
    Cast add-row on (xs).
Done.
State table.
